{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' answer/launch_recommendation.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Checkpoint 3: Launch Recommendation\n\nRecommend launching the first wave with exactly these three clinics: Maple Junction Clinic, Riverbend Health, and Hillcrest Annex. These are the only clinics that satisfy all current hard requirements for region, open status, accepted storage status, full coordinator coverage for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14, delivery by 2026-06-07, and budget fit.\n\nTotal rollout cost is `$18,800`, leaving `$1,200` remaining from the `$20,000` first-wave budget.\n\nAnchor clinic and continuity code: Maple Junction Clinic remains eligible, so it stays the donor continuity anchor. Donor continuity code: `MJ-14`.\n\n| Selected clinic | Carrier | Delivery date | Total rollout cost |\n| --- | --- | --- | ---: |\n| Maple Junction Clinic | SwiftRoute | 2026-06-06 | $7,400 |\n| Riverbend Health | NorthLine | 2026-06-07 | $6,450 |\n| Hillcrest Annex | Valley Freight | 2026-06-07 | $4,950 |\n\nRejected-clinic summary:\n\n- Pine Ridge Outreach was excluded because coordinator coverage fails on 2026-06-12.\n- Lakeside Family Care was excluded because storage is suspended and retest is after the launch period.\n- Cedar Works Clinic was excluded because the clinic is closed for maintenance and transport misses the delivery cutoff.\n- Old Mill Clinic was excluded because storage remains `conditional pass pending`.\n- South Gate Clinic was excluded because it is outside the North region.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
